## BOTTOM LINE

The machine can move the price in milliseconds.

The physical economy cannot move at that speed.

Fair value cannot be repealed by momentum.

Oil cannot be talked lower forever.

Debt cannot be financed by a green candle.

The bond market cannot be made irrelevant because equities refuse to listen.

Household purchasing power cannot be replaced by market capitalization.

And a correction cannot be permanently erased without preserving the imbalance that made the correction necessary.

**THE INDEX IS THE DISPLAY.**

**THE PHYSICAL ECONOMY IS THE STRUCTURE.**

**WHEN THE TWO SEPARATE FAR ENOUGH, THE SEPARATION ITSELF BECOMES THE WARNING.**
